h(19, 400, """No creature has ever committed injustice on earth except by inventing a right from his own mind and deluding himself that it is his right!""")

t(19, 1005, """Injustice comes in types, classes and forms.
And it is astonishing that, if we look at the class of a husband's mother's injustice toward her son's wife, we find:
The first type
🔴 🔥🔥🔥🔥 Muslim mothers-in-law are drowning up to their ears in oppressing their sons' wives, (((except those on whom Allah has mercy and whom He guides)))!! The oppression of oppressive Muslim mothers-in-law can stretch over 365 days of the year!! Muslims .. meaning they pray 5 times .. Muslims .. meaning they know there is a Fire!! Muslims .. meaning they have read in the Book of Allah the Exalted that the end of injustice is the Fire!

The second type
🟢 Non-Muslim mothers-in-law .. Christians .. Buddhists, Confucians and atheists. Because of the great social transformations, with children absent from the parents' city, scattered across the earth and living all year without contact with the families of either side, the spring of the mother-in-law's oppression of her son's wife is dry. But, as Allah has willed, it gushes with stagnant water in the Muslim society that repeats night and day headings such as: family ties .. kindness to parents by clinging to them geographically. Yet this very society slides, through these indisputable shar'i headings, down unethical behavioral slopes. So we find that unbelieving women have escaped one type of oppression, while Muslim women drown in it: Muslim mothers-in-law practising oppression every day, and no husbands to deter them! The role and manhood of the father-in-law, the mother-in-law's husband, is completely absent; silent, mute, as if the one practising oppression is not someone he will be held accountable for on the Day of Resurrection, forgetting that she is his wife and that he is accountable for her conduct on the Day of Resurrection because of his guardianship over her.

This is among the wonders of the Muslims' decline in the time of the end!""")

h(19, 2200, """It is among what stirs wonder!""")

t(20, 335, """That a Muslim speaks to me time and again, and in nearly every one of those times, whenever he talks and speaks, he says, repeats and reiterates: "I trust you!" May Allah forgive every Muslim man and woman who does not intend harm, and that is my constant opinion of every Muslim man and woman. But the matter, when repeated, turns into a clear feeling in the listener that he is under constant evaluation by a person who is himself only human, and the feeling grows worse when something like this is repeated time and again, until the listener says to himself: Do I even care in the first place what his view of me is, this or that?!

Praise be to Allah, and then ..
If a person has grown up, been raised and shaped while rejecting being drawn into the herd culture since the age of 7, this person became independent very early. So can a person who has lived most of his life independent, whether man or woman, care who trusts him and who does not? People's opinion of him is, in the first place, = minus 866436754335644654

It is hurtful, even with good intentions, to make a person feel time and again that he is waiting for someone's opinion of him, while he regards anyone's opinion of him as something he does not even think about. For the person who is independent through Allah the Exalted is not like one who lives within the herd, whose opinion of him concerns this one, and who fears that one may think this or that of him! The independent person is not concerned with any of this at all. So I felt great astonishment, to the point of hurt, today at the continuation of this style in communication. And I apologise for saying: the last thing in existence that concerns me is for a person to say to me "I trust you!" I understand it being said once, that is natural, but when it is repeated and repeated and repeated it becomes hurtful and gives the listener a false signal that he lives waiting for someone to trust him!""")

h(20, 1400, """It is among what hurts!""")

t(20, 2075, """The servants of Allah have seen dreams since a time we do not know, perhaps since the day our father Adam descended to earth, and yet in every age the know-it-alls live who hear nothing but the voices coming from inside their own minds!

This is a situation and a human experience so that the know-it-alls understand that the truth is not in their minds. The truth is from Allah the Exalted, only, only and only.

Long years ago I was urged to wear out my soul and body collecting money to buy property in Gaza, and I always used to reply: Gaza is a land of ribat, not a land of life and settlement. So I was exposed to criticism. Then I saw the whole land in a dream 12 years ago as rubble, all of it stones piled on top of one another, and I said: this will happen and this will befall the land. And there came mockery, accusations of madness and accusations of foolishness!

Who is right today?

To the know-it-alls who listen only to the voices coming from inside their heads: How long will you stay like this?! Is it not time for you to change?!""")

