t(32, 800, """Ask the Lord for gentleness and mercy, for most people do not know of their Lord what, if they knew it, would rob them of sweet sleep, since their understanding of their Lord has scarcely any known existence within themselves.. Most people are truly heedless of their Lord's signs in villages and peoples.

Many a Muslim in the farthest corners of the earth has striven in supplication for a people and a village out of love of good for them, and they relapsed to lower than what they were in. So O people of the villages, wherever you live: rain is withheld only by sins and desires, lording it over the weak, and arrogance of the self; by all of these blessings are obliterated, supplications are not answered, mercies do not descend, and provisions sink like water sinking into the ground, sought yet out of reach of hands. So fear Allah regarding yourselves, fear Allah regarding your provisions and your children's provisions, and fear Allah regarding your lives. For provision is a helper at the stations of gratitude, praise and humility. And that is not by the tongue at all; rather, thanking Allah is as He commanded and made clear, and that is only by humility on earth, good character, refraining from harm, and upholding the truth among people. If people refuse, it is their certain destruction, and then they can blame only themselves.""")

h(32, 1700, """If Allah hates a village or a people, the provisions of its people perish, and they perish in it!""")

t(32, 2300, """The truth has opened the file of the whole Ummah .. a 20-year-old girl in Pakistan accused of zina without witnesses and without being given a chance to defend herself .. a dangerous file whose title is: a section of Muslims inventing a new religion that the Prophet ﷺ and his family did not bring, embracing it and applying it by force of arms, throwing the words of their Mighty Lord, the Compeller, the King, and His commands and prohibitions against the wall, and inventing punishments and hudud of their own making!!""")

h(33, 400, """The killing of the Pakistani Khalida Shandio: reopening the file of tribal councils and the sins and crimes of these councils!""")

t(33, 1015, """To those whose supplications have been delayed in being answered for years while they wait, there are several matters: among people are those whose supplication is answered with better than what they asked for, in Paradise, so better than what he asked for in this world is stored up for him. And there are those whose supplication is answered after a year, or five years, or ten years, or twenty years. Whoever finds the answer to his supplication delayed should know that there are those whose answer has been delayed more than his! And I have, in the experience of patience over the answering of supplication, something worth telling, perhaps the reader will benefit: between 2015 and 2016 I went through an extremely hard, bitter experience; it demolished my entire previous life completely, not partially, and my present life, which I live today, actually began in 2017 as a clear, firm life line with no crookedness in it.

Since 2015 and 2016 were extremely heavy and represented unprecedented hardship, the period from mid-2015 to mid-2016 was a stage of great striving in the supplication of the night prayer; I left nothing I wished for in this world and the Hereafter without calling upon the Lord of the worlds for it, the King, the Mighty, holy are His names and attributes, magnified in the heavens and on earth, exalted greatly. And as is the habit of the weak human being, he calls upon his Lord, hopes for the answer, and his soul waits, but something happened that changed the equation!

In November 2016, in Malaysia, the station of the land of distress, for three visits to it represented three great distresses, in that month of 2016, while I was in the second station of distress (2010 - 2016 - 2024), carrying in my breast many supplications I had made to our Mighty Lord, I saw the Prophet ﷺ in a dream standing on a place raised about 5 cm from the ground; he was standing while I sat directly before him. To my right and left were men all wearing white, strangers I did not know, with metres between me and them to the right and left (perhaps 5 metres). The Prophet ﷺ addressed us all and told us what I want the reader to understand now, and it is the essence of the experience.. I had made many supplications, and the dream came not for me alone but for other Muslims too, so that the Prophet ﷺ could address us with a single address, saying: "All that you supplicated for has been answered for you, but in its time."

This great dream was a major turning point for me in my understanding of the decrees of Allah the Exalted. I understood, learned and realised that it is not right for us, not fitting, not permissible, not our right, not expected of us, and our Lord is not pleased with us, to hasten the answer, or to insist on asking for it to be hastened, or to ask about the reason for its delay; that all of this is error, mistake, lack of understanding, and a failure to perceive the purposes of Allah the Exalted in His servants and on the earth we live upon and in which we live the decrees of the Mighty Lord.

For this reason I no longer hasten. In ten years, of the supplications, Allah knows best, 1 to 10% have been answered. And the reason for ignorance of how much of the supplication was answered is that man is so ignorant of the unseen of Allah hidden from him, even in his own life; it is a real ignorance confirming the reality of the creature's value of nothingness before the decrees of Allah the Exalted, such that he may not even be able to calculate precisely how much of his supplication was answered. And in view of all this, as a humble servant of Allah the Exalted, in need of Him, I continue to make most of the same supplications since that very dream (2016 - 2026), over which a little less than ten years have now passed. For it is never fitting for us to cut off supplication, and it is never right to cut off seeking means to the Mighty Lord even if we were given glad tidings that our supplications were answered. For the answering is one matter, and continuing the supplication is another. However long the answer of the supplication is delayed, call upon Allah the Exalted, and do not stop even if you are given glad tidings that your supplication has been answered. Do not hasten, do not resent, do not grumble, do not be displeased, and do not despair so that you stop supplicating and abandon the great worship of supplication, and become one of the regretful.""")

h(34, 400, """“Indeed, Allah is with the patient” — to those who hasten the answering of supplication and are not patient!""")

t(34, 1015, """My son, my daughter: take it from me, and cut short the certain pains of everyone who is displeased with the purposes of Allah on earth! We are two creations that do not resemble each other in dozens of things. The man who looks at a woman and sees himself with a woman's face is mad, and the woman who looks in the mirror and finds herself with a man's face is mad!

Allah the Exalted created us as two creations, not one creation .. hundreds of millions of men and women lived, then died and left the world, not knowing this which I say!

What I say is knowledge that is obligatory to know; it is not a luxury of knowledge, nor one of the moulds of entertainment through optional reading! The matter is great, and it is the cause of the corruption of most women's minds and the corruption of most men's minds!

The man who thinks that Allah the Exalted created the woman's soul like his own is a man in need of learning the obligatory knowledge, and the woman who thinks that Allah the Exalted created the man's soul like her own is a woman in need of learning the obligatory knowledge!

Ignorance has struck most people a blow and brought them down, obliterated their minds, and left them without understanding, without knowledge, without perception and without comprehension. Ignorance covered them and became their cloak; wisdom was withheld from them, so they dwelt in the abode of those who wronged themselves, and Allah did not wrong them. All this because their Lord commanded them to learn, and they refused all but ignorance.

We are two creations: in soul we do not resemble each other, in mind we do not resemble each other, in aims we do not resemble each other, and we have nothing in common except perception and conscience!""")

